Z||000000||hutch84fierose||09-25-2001||06:33 AM||||Alright now i have an 84 se and gonna put a gt rear bumper on the car i have looked on the forum and every one has different opinions on how to do this thats why i am asking.  For sure whats the way to do this????  What do i need to do and get????<BR>everyone is talking about totally different things thats all.  from you just bolt off and bolt on.  is that the case or you need to get different parts i have no idea<BR>thanks for the help||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||09-25-2001||01:14 PM||||I havent done it but I think you have to change tail lites too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||09-25-2001||01:18 PM||||If you're just replacing the lower fascia... all you'll need is the part itself, and the impact absorber "honeycomb" that fits inside it.  You'd only need to change the taillights if you were switching from a notchback to a fastback.  Should be an easy process.  The other thing that might not match up is the trim... 84's had "grooved" trim, where later models had smooth trim.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||09-25-2001||01:35 PM||||You won't have to change the tail lights but you will have to take them out.  The screws that hold them in are under the 6 black caps behind the trunk.  You'll need to remove the rear corner lights (torx screws) and the 7mm screws behind them.  You'll need GT wheelwell liners, however you can make a filler piece from spare fender liners to fill the open corner.  You'll also need a plastic bracket that goes from the spaceframe to the rivets at bottom of the bumper.  Across the top of the bumper (under the tail lights) are more rivets.  The rivets release by pulling up the center with a screwdriver.<P>Ribbed mouldings were on '84 indys and '85 GT's/SE's and possibly '86 notchbacks.<P>To make everything look and sound great, you'll eventually want to add dual exhaust.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 09-25-2001).]||||reg||1
